$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }t\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{2})+(\goldD{15})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac{17}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f\left(\blueD{\dfrac{17}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
f\left(\blueD{\dfrac{17}{2}}\right)&=-\left(\blueD{\dfrac{17}{2}}-2\right)\left(\blueD{\dfrac{17}{2}}-15\right)
\\\\
&=-\left(\dfrac{13}{2}\right)\left(-\dfrac{13}{2}\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{169}{4}
\end{align}$
